      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "### Getting Started with NexusCore\n\nTo begin using NexusCore, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Authenticate**: Start by obtaining an access token using the `POST /auth/token` endpoint. This will return a JSON Web Token (JWT) that you can use to authenticate subsequent requests.\n2. **Make a GET Request**: Once authenticated, make a GET request to the `/v1/data` endpoint to retrieve a sample dataset. This will return a JSON response containing the data in a human-readable format.\n3. **Handle Errors**: NexusCore returns HTTP status codes to indicate the outcome of each request. Refer to the [Error Codes](#error-codes) section for a list of common error codes and their corresponding descriptions.\n\n### Example Code\n\nHere's an example of how to make a GET request using the `curl` command:\n```bash\ncurl -X GET \\\n  https://nexuscore.example.com/v1/data \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN'\n```\n### Error Codes\n\n| Error Code | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| 401 | Unauthorized |\n| 404 | Resource Not Found |\n| 500 | Internal Server Error |\n\nBy following these steps, you'll be well on your",
