      "content": "### Getting Started with NexusCore\n\nTo begin using NexusCore, follow these steps:\n\n#### Step 1: Obtain an Access Token\n\nTo authenticate with NexusCore, you'll need to obtain an access token using the `POST /auth/token` endpoint. This endpoint accepts a JSON payload with the following properties:\n\n* `username`: The username of the user making the request.\n* `password`: The password of the user making the request.\n* `client_id`: The client ID of the application making the request.\n* `client_secret`: The client secret of the application making the request.\n\nHere's an example of the payload:\n```json\n{\n  \"username\": \"your_username\",\n  \"password\": \"your_password\",\n  \"client_id\": \"your_client_id\",\n  \"client_secret\": \"your_client_secret\"\n}\n```\nSend a `POST` request to the `/auth/token` endpoint with the payload in the request body. The response will contain a JSON Web Token (JWT) that you can use to authenticate subsequent requests.\n\n#### Step 2: Make a GET Request\n\nOnce you have an access token, you can make a GET request to the `/v1/data` endpoint to retrieve a sample dataset. Here are the",
